1
00:00:22,884 --> 00:00:24,364
我超酷的家人
My super-awesome family

2
00:00:24,364 --> 00:00:27,344
提前给我办了一个生日惊喜聚会
was throwing me a surprise early birthday party.

3
00:00:27,384 --> 00:00:29,264
我猜只有我一个人在家
I'm guess I'm the only one at home.

4
00:00:29,264 --> 00:00:29,794
老爸 你怎么能这样
How could you do this?! Dad!

5
00:00:29,794 --> 00:00:31,584
你本该是我的英雄
You were supposed to be my hero!

6
00:00:31,744 --> 00:00:33,044
你真让我失望
You let me down!

7
00:00:33,044 --> 00:00:35,795
或者我今天忘了找电工
Or I forgot to meet the electrician today

8
00:00:35,795 --> 00:00:37,995
修家里的接线盒
to fix our faulty junction box.

9
00:00:38,795 --> 00:00:40,735
各位 我不会找借口
Guys, I'm not gonna make excuses.

10
00:00:40,735 --> 00:00:42,275
我上班真太忙了
I've been really busy at work.

11
00:00:42,275 --> 00:00:44,085
我拉头发刚拉到一半
Well, I was halfway through straightening my hair.

12
00:00:44,095 --> 00:00:44,975
我正在洗
And I was in the middle

13
00:00:44,985 --> 00:00:46,525
攒了三周的衣服
of doing three weeks' worth of laundry.

14
00:00:46,525 --> 00:00:48,525
而我刚才真的写期末论文
And I was actually writing a term paper

15
00:00:48,525 --> 00:00:51,106
灯就灭了 然后 什么
right when the lights went out, and...what?

16
00:00:51,106 --> 00:00:52,336
这不是苏打水啊
This isn't soda.

17
00:00:52,336 --> 00:00:53,596
好了 趁你们还没发表任何意见
Okay, before you guys say anything,

18
00:00:53,596 --> 00:00:56,086
我穿这件衣服是因为我实在没...
I only put this on because I didn't have anything --

19
00:00:58,986 --> 00:01:01,196
看来问题自己解决了
Well, the problem obviously self-corrected,

20
00:01:01,196 --> 00:01:02,817
我早料到了
which I knew it would.

21
00:01:02,847 --> 00:01:04,087
是我修好的
Well, I fixed it.

22
00:01:04,087 --> 00:01:05,237
老妈叫人来修了
Yeah, mom called a guy.

23
00:01:05,237 --> 00:01:08,187
克莱尔 抱歉 我太忙了
Oh, Claire, I'm so sorry. I got busy at work, and --

24
00:01:08,187 --> 00:01:10,017
亲爱的 别在意
Oh, honey, don't even worry about it.

25
00:01:10,207 --> 00:01:12,177
还好冰箱又能工作了
I'm just glad the fridge is up and running.

26
00:01:12,177 --> 00:01:14,447
我把明天的午饭提前备好了
I pre-packed all the lunches for tomorrow.

27
00:01:14,447 --> 00:01:16,938
三明治里的布里奶酪可别化了
I didn't want the Brie on the sandwiches to get runny.

28
00:01:16,938 --> 00:01:17,688
布里奶酪
Brie?

29
00:01:17,688 --> 00:01:18,918
别再剧透了
Don't tell me any more.

30
00:01:18,918 --> 00:01:19,978
要的就是惊喜
I live for the surprise.

31
00:01:19,978 --> 00:01:22,158
老妈 我知道你工作忙 不过
Hey, Mom, I know you're really busy at work, but --

32
00:01:22,158 --> 00:01:24,528
甜心 我绝不会拿这个当借口
Sweetheart, I would never use that as an excuse.

33
00:01:24,528 --> 00:01:25,308
有什么指示
What do you need?

34
00:01:25,308 --> 00:01:26,828
-卖糕饼用的纸杯蛋糕 -好哇
- The cupcakes for the bake sale. - Okay.

35
00:01:26,828 --> 00:01:28,268
我们刚被困在家里
Oh, and since we got stuck here,

36
00:01:28,268 --> 00:01:29,168
没法出门
I couldn't go out and get

37
00:01:29,168 --> 00:01:30,299
给我室友买生日礼物
that birthday present for my roommate.

38
00:01:30,299 --> 00:01:31,819
也没法去干洗店拿裙子
Or my dress from the dry cleaners.

39
00:01:31,819 --> 00:01:34,509
遵命 遵命 遵命
Done, done, and done.

40
00:01:34,509 --> 00:01:36,399
-妈妈最棒了 -抱抱
- We have the best mom ever. - Hugs!

41
00:01:36,749 --> 00:01:37,439
好吧
Okay.

42
00:01:37,439 --> 00:01:39,739
等等 大伙儿 老爸在这呢
Wait, wait, guys. Guys, Dad's here.

43
00:01:39,879 --> 00:01:41,989
老爸 拍一张我们抱老妈的照片
Dad, take a photo of us hugging Mom.

44
00:01:42,709 --> 00:01:44,500
以前我把家事搞砸的时候
Until now, when I'd screw up on the home front,

45
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:45,830
总可以拿工作当借口
I could always blame work,

46
00:01:45,830 --> 00:01:47,090
可现在克莱尔要经营公司
but with Claire running a company

47
00:01:47,090 --> 00:01:48,270
妈妈这个角色当得前所未有的称职
and being a better mom than ever,

48
00:01:48,270 --> 00:01:49,630
我都能感受到孩子们
I could feel the kids downgrading

49
00:01:49,630 --> 00:01:51,070
对我大失所望了
their whole opinion of me.

50
00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:53,320
从A级老爸变成F级了
I went from an "A" Dad to an "F" Dad.

51
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:57,461
废·邓菲 菲尔·邓废
Fail Dunphy. Phil Dun-fail.

52
00:01:58,201 --> 00:02:00,571
废利普·很废 邓...
Failip Hum-fail Dun--

53
00:02:00,571 --> 00:02:02,351
我以前说很溜的
No, I had it before.

54
00:02:02,361 --> 00:02:03,321
说"布里"
Say "Brie."

55
00:02:03,321 --> 00:02:04,661
布里
Brie!

56
00:02:04,661 --> 00:02:05,751
我觉得啊
Hey, you know what?

57
00:02:05,751 --> 00:02:08,171
明天我也可以帮帮孩子们
I could do some of that kid stuff tomorrow.

58
00:02:08,221 --> 00:02:09,861
你有开放参观日要忙呢
You've got that open house.

59
00:02:09,861 --> 00:02:12,712
亲爱的 我都跟工作和家庭周旋22年了
Honey, I've been juggling work and family for 22 years

60
00:02:12,712 --> 00:02:14,112
这点事情算什么
and just juggling for 30.

61
00:02:14,112 --> 00:02:16,022
那条裙子我到时候得穿 所以
Well, I really need that dress for an event, so --

62
00:02:16,022 --> 00:02:17,092
交给我
I got it.

63
00:02:17,092 --> 00:02:19,412
明天的任务 拿裙子
Agenda for tomorrow -- One dress,

64
00:02:19,462 --> 00:02:23,272
做蛋糕 买礼物 没了
one set of cupcakes, one present, and that's it.

65
00:02:23,272 --> 00:02:25,513
我记住了 别以为我会忘
I got ya! You thought I forgot.

66
00:02:25,523 --> 00:02:29,393
我3点40就去找警报公司的人来
I will be here to meet the alarm company at precisely 3:40...

67
00:02:30,543 --> 00:02:32,073
今天3点40就该找的
earlier today.

68
00:02:47,354 --> 00:02:49,144
昨晚还没吵够吗
You didn't make enough noise last night?

69
00:02:49,344 --> 00:02:51,805
他哭得我失眠四个小时
With all his crying, I didn't sleep four hours.

70
00:02:51,805 --> 00:02:52,955
我也没合眼
I didn't close my eyes.

71
00:02:52,955 --> 00:02:54,485
感觉像回到我的村子
It was like being back in my village,

72
00:02:54,485 --> 00:02:55,705
警惕土匪来一样
watching for the marauders.

73
00:02:55,705 --> 00:02:56,925
我也不知道哪个更让我惊讶
I don't know what's more shocking --

74
00:02:56,925 --> 00:02:58,955
你原来要站岗放哨还是会用"土匪"这个词了
You standing watch, or knowing the word "Marauders."

75
00:02:58,955 --> 00:03:00,945
别跟我说我小时候
Please tell me I didn't sob all night

76
00:03:00,945 --> 00:03:02,775
因为小毯子不见了哭了一整晚
just 'cause I lost my baby blanket.

77
00:03:02,775 --> 00:03:04,716
嘘 别让他想起来 他现在挺开心的
Shh! Don't remind him. He's happy now.

78
00:03:04,716 --> 00:03:06,646
再说 你小时候连毯子都没有
And besides, you didn't even have a blanket.

79
00:03:06,646 --> 00:03:08,316
咱们以前一贫如洗
We were basically destitute.

80
00:03:08,326 --> 00:03:09,686
怎么 你们家被闪电击中了吗
What, did you get hit by lightning?

81
00:03:09,686 --> 00:03:11,816
还好乔今天约好要跟小朋友出去玩
Thank God that Joe has a playdate.

82
00:03:11,816 --> 00:03:13,106
维吉会来接我们
Vicky's picking us up.

83
00:03:13,116 --> 00:03:15,166
我要让他狠狠玩
I'm gonna make him play so hard

84
00:03:15,166 --> 00:03:17,036
玩到今晚累晕
that he's gonna pass out tonight.

85
00:03:17,036 --> 00:03:18,797
我跟威士忌有个约会
Well, I've got a playdate with Johnnie Walker,

86
00:03:18,797 --> 00:03:20,847
我俩中的一个今晚会不省人事
so one of us is passing out tonight.

87
00:03:21,747 --> 00:03:23,217
好啦 我知道没狗粮了
Yeah, I know we're out of dog food.

88
00:03:23,217 --> 00:03:24,657
我打完高尔夫就去买
I'll pick some up after golf.

89
00:03:24,657 --> 00:03:26,557
她正好可以借此机会减肥 没事
She could lose a couple of pounds, anyways.

90
00:03:26,567 --> 00:03:28,237
还好你没女儿
Thank God you don't have a daughter.

91
00:03:30,227 --> 00:03:31,908
等那孩子一睡着
The minute that kid falls asleep,

92
00:03:31,908 --> 00:03:34,268
我保证那架飞机一定失联
that plane goes Amelia Earhart.

93
00:03:35,628 --> 00:03:37,598
这布置是不是感觉挺低端的
Doesn't this seem a little chintzy?

94
00:03:37,598 --> 00:03:38,808
是啊 咱们可以走了吗
Yeah, can we go now?

95
00:03:38,808 --> 00:03:40,828
不行 还没跟两位新郎问好呢
No, we haven't said hello to the grooms --

96
00:03:40,828 --> 00:03:43,828
还有策划这场婚礼的才子
Or the talented people who planned this wedding.

97
00:03:43,828 --> 00:03:45,789
胡娇·萨尔兹曼的又一力作 伙计们
Another great Pepper Saltzman production, guys.

98
00:03:45,789 --> 00:03:49,149
得了吧 周五中午的婚礼简直俗到家了
Oh, please. What's tackier than a Friday lunch wedding?

99
00:03:49,509 --> 00:03:52,479
给五号桌拿点 番茄酱
Table five needs more...ketchup.

100
00:03:53,249 --> 00:03:54,669
每次摄影师过来
I have to hide my face with a coat

101
00:03:54,669 --> 00:03:56,469
我都得拿外套遮脸
every time the videographer comes around.

102
00:03:56,469 --> 00:03:57,199
想当年
In the old days,

103
00:03:57,199 --> 00:03:59,170
他从不接这么便宜的单
he'd never taken a cheap job like this,

104
00:03:59,170 --> 00:04:01,310
可是同性恋婚礼越来越少了
but the gay-wedding business is drying up.

105
00:04:01,310 --> 00:04:05,480
我们会把便宜婚礼统一办成谢曼·萨尔兹曼婚典
We do the bargain ones as Sherman Saltzman Events,

106
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:06,850
然而35年前我在卢博克搭上那辆公车后
and I haven't been Sherman

107
00:04:06,850 --> 00:04:09,410
就没用过谢曼这个名字了
since I got on that bus in Lubbock 35 years ago.

108
00:04:09,410 --> 00:04:11,580
都好几个月了才订了另外两场
We've only booked two others in months --

109
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:13,151
上周亚当和迈克的婚礼
Adam and Michael last weekend

110
00:04:13,151 --> 00:04:15,831
和下周一菲利克斯和乔丹的
and Felix and Jordan next Monday.

111
00:04:15,901 --> 00:04:16,931
周一
Monday.

112
00:04:17,271 --> 00:04:19,141
走开 阴魂不散的
Oh, away, you vulture.

113
00:04:20,231 --> 00:04:21,631
小卡 你会不会觉得有点奇怪
Cam, do you think it's a little weird --

114
00:04:21,631 --> 00:04:23,481
亚当和迈克 菲利克斯和乔丹的婚礼
That we weren't invited to Adam and Michael's

115
00:04:23,481 --> 00:04:25,391
都没请我们 是的 非常怪
or Felix and Jordan's? Yes. Totally weird.

116
00:04:25,391 --> 00:04:26,752
亲爱的 小孩坐这桌
Okay, sweetie, here's the kid's table.

117
00:04:26,752 --> 00:04:29,312
我们该坐哪儿 没有空位了
Where is our table? There are no more tables.

118
00:04:29,502 --> 00:04:30,792
我的天
Oh, my God.

119
00:04:31,062 --> 00:04:33,002
我们要坐那里 65号桌
That's us. Number 65.

120
00:04:33,002 --> 00:04:34,542
我们的朋友呢
Where are our friends?

121
00:04:34,552 --> 00:04:35,512
都不在这里
Not here.

122
00:04:36,122 --> 00:04:38,432
我们是被列入基佬黑名单了吗
Are we on some sort of gay blacklist?

123
00:04:39,983 --> 00:04:41,113
-我不要坐那儿 -你坐那儿
- I'm not sitting there. - You're sitting there.

124
00:04:43,643 --> 00:04:44,403
你好
Hello.

125
00:04:44,403 --> 00:04:45,273
你好 亲爱的
Hey, honey.

126
00:04:45,293 --> 00:04:47,413
记得纸杯蛋糕 礼物 还有裙子
Oh, cupcakes, present, dress.

127
00:04:47,413 --> 00:04:48,773
我记着呢 我马上去办
I remember. I'm gonna get on that

128
00:04:48,773 --> 00:04:50,293
等我先把这边布置完
just as soon as I'm done with my open house.

129
00:04:50,293 --> 00:04:52,913
先问一下 礼物要到哪里去拿
I just wanted to clarify, where am I getting the present?

130
00:04:53,414 --> 00:04:54,284
等一下 菲尔
Hang on, Phil.

131
00:04:54,284 --> 00:04:55,864
我这边在忙
I'm in the middle of something.

132
00:04:56,804 --> 00:04:58,044
等我一下下
Just one second.

133
00:04:58,044 --> 00:05:01,524
你要去百思买商场找斯但 斯坦
I'm -- it's at the Best Buy. Ask for S-Sean -- Stan.

134
00:05:01,524 --> 00:05:02,354
说是邓菲家订的
It's under "Dunphy".

135
00:05:02,354 --> 00:05:03,324
谢谢亲爱的
Thanks, honey.

136
00:05:03,534 --> 00:05:04,854
真不知道你怎么能记住这么多东西
I don't know how you do it all.

137
00:05:04,944 --> 00:05:06,074
爱你
Love you.

138
00:05:07,205 --> 00:05:08,145
那是个提土旁吗
That's a "t"?

139
00:05:08,145 --> 00:05:10,395
人们说要持好家和管好公司
They say it takes a village to raise a family

140
00:05:10,395 --> 00:05:11,755
通常需要很多人齐心协力
and run a company.

141
00:05:12,225 --> 00:05:13,585
原来 要实现这一切
Turns out, it just takes

142
00:05:13,585 --> 00:05:15,845
只需要市场部一个叫本的马屁精
one little suck-up from marketing named Ben.

143
00:05:16,475 --> 00:05:17,695
克莱尔 不知道你有没有听说
Oh, Claire, I don't know if you heard.

144
00:05:17,695 --> 00:05:19,675
他们把克莱默的会议提前到五点了
They moved the Kramer meeting back to 5:00.

145
00:05:19,675 --> 00:05:20,395
-不 -是的
- No. - Yeah.

146
00:05:20,406 --> 00:05:23,276
不行 我要给卢克球队做千层面晚餐
No, I-I have to make a lasagna for Luke's team dinner,

147
00:05:23,396 --> 00:05:24,376
但是我也不能错过这个会议
but I can't miss that meeting.

148
00:05:24,376 --> 00:05:25,746
其实我是厨房好手
You know, I know my way around a kitchen.

149
00:05:25,756 --> 00:05:26,766
因为我妈是个酒鬼
My mom's an alcoholic.

150
00:05:26,766 --> 00:05:28,816
所以我能轻松帮你做好千层面
So I could easily knock out a lasagna for you.

151
00:05:28,816 --> 00:05:31,526
本 你救了我一命
Ben, you are a lifesaver.

152
00:05:31,666 --> 00:05:33,886
我保证不会老麻烦你帮我忙
I promise I will not make a habit of it.

153
00:05:33,886 --> 00:05:35,307
其实我真想一直让他帮忙
I kind of made a habit of it.

154
00:05:35,827 --> 00:05:36,827
淡定点
Calm down.

155
00:05:36,827 --> 00:05:38,547
我们只是翘了两节课
We only cut two classes,

156
00:05:38,547 --> 00:05:41,457
我会用你妈妈的电脑发一封请假邮件
and I'll send an excuse e-mail from your mom's computer.

157
00:05:41,457 --> 00:05:42,987
真不敢相信就因为你给我半个布里奶酪三明治
I can't believe I agreed to ditch with you

158
00:05:42,987 --> 00:05:45,097
我就答应跟着你翘课了
just 'cause you gave me half your Brie sandwich.

159
00:05:45,097 --> 00:05:46,827
不过那里面味道超好的苹果片
Although that party-crashing apple slice

160
00:05:46,827 --> 00:05:48,728
给三明治增色不少
turned out to be a welcome plus-one.

161
00:05:48,728 --> 00:05:50,358
那我们现在可以摊开说了吧
So we can make it official now.

162
00:05:50,358 --> 00:05:52,108
其实我有三个基佬舅舅[包括曼尼]
I have three gay uncles.

163
00:05:53,468 --> 00:05:54,768
是的 我很抱歉 迈尔斯
Yeah, I'm -- I'm sorry, Miles.

164
00:05:54,768 --> 00:05:56,248
不 帮我跟大家道个歉
No, apologize to the guys.

165
00:05:56,248 --> 00:05:58,338
我只是太累了 打不了高尔夫
It's just, I'm too tired to play golf.

166
00:05:59,778 --> 00:06:01,519
该死 忘了买狗粮
Damn it! The dog food!

167
00:06:08,069 --> 00:06:10,149
斯黛拉 你今天走运了
Stella, this is your lucky day.

168
00:06:10,189 --> 00:06:12,009
我和歌洛莉亚第一次约会的时候
Gloria makes this Colombian dish

169
00:06:12,019 --> 00:06:13,989
她做过一道我爱吃的哥伦比亚菜
I loved when we were first dating.

170
00:06:15,450 --> 00:06:17,290
其实那时候我也说过其它的谎
I lied about a lot of things back then.

171
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:24,000
你在干嘛
What the hell are you doing?!

172
00:06:24,830 --> 00:06:27,220
我花了三天
That takes me three days!

173
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:28,941
三天来准备这道菜
Three days to prepare!

174
00:06:28,941 --> 00:06:30,791
然后你说你很爱吃
And then you say that you love it,

175
00:06:30,791 --> 00:06:32,361
现在你竟然把它拿去喂狗
and you feed it to the dog?

176
00:06:32,361 --> 00:06:34,101
你还骗了我什么
What else have you been lying about,

177
00:06:34,101 --> 00:06:35,551
杰·肯尼迪·普里契特
Jay Kennedy Pritchett?

178
00:06:38,021 --> 00:06:40,601
斯黛拉吃掉这菜后这周都不能跟我亲亲了
No Daddy kisses till Sunday after she eats this.

179
00:06:40,601 --> 00:06:41,781
对不起 维奇
Sorry, Vicky.

180
00:06:41,781 --> 00:06:43,742
今天孩子们不能一起玩了
We have to cancel the playdate.

181
00:06:43,742 --> 00:06:46,312
乔在车里睡着了 我不想吵醒他
Joe fell asleep in the car, and I don't want to wake him up.

182
00:06:47,032 --> 00:06:47,862
好的
Okay.

183
00:06:48,232 --> 00:06:49,982
杰出去打高尔夫了真是万幸
Thank God that Jay was out playing golf.

184
00:06:49,982 --> 00:06:52,522
上一次乔睡着了我把他忘在车里
The last time that I left Joe sleeping in the car...

185
00:06:52,982 --> 00:06:53,812
亲爱的 乔呢
Honey, where's Joe?

186
00:06:53,812 --> 00:06:54,952
在车里睡着呢
Sleeping in the car.

187
00:06:54,952 --> 00:06:56,003
你疯了吗
Are you crazy?!

188
00:06:56,003 --> 00:06:57,573
你不能把小孩留在车里
You don't leave a kid in the car!

189
00:06:57,573 --> 00:06:58,623
你怎么不干脆在他身上放个标志
Why don't you just put a sign on him

190
00:06:58,623 --> 00:07:00,373
再写上"免费土狼食物"
saying "Free Coyote Food"?!

191
00:07:00,613 --> 00:07:02,763
我没见过谁发这么大的脾气
I have never seen anyone so mad.

192
00:07:02,793 --> 00:07:05,383
就算是抢匪 起码你还能跟他对上话
Even the marauders, you could have a conversation with.

193
00:07:05,623 --> 00:07:07,283
"家里有急事"
"Family Emergency."

194
00:07:07,293 --> 00:07:09,874
"叽里呱啦 歌洛莉亚·普里契特"
"Blah, blah, blah. Gloria Pritchett."

195
00:07:09,874 --> 00:07:11,274
然后发送
And send.

196
00:07:11,274 --> 00:07:12,744
我真不想问出口
I hate that I have to ask this,

197
00:07:12,744 --> 00:07:14,924
但你不是真的把"叽里呱啦"打上去了吧
but you didn't type "Blah, blah, blah," did you?

198
00:07:14,954 --> 00:07:16,004
你得放松
You need to chill...

199
00:07:16,284 --> 00:07:17,724
像我女朋友这样
like my girlfriend here.

200
00:07:20,884 --> 00:07:21,904
不 我受不了这个
Nah, I can't enjoy that.

201
00:07:21,914 --> 00:07:23,745
我一直会想到那女孩的爸爸
I just keep thinking about that girl's father.

202
00:07:23,755 --> 00:07:25,815
你能不能别在我妈的电脑上播这玩意
Could you please just get that off my mom's computer?

203
00:07:25,815 --> 00:07:28,085
好吧 这是给你翘课的奖励
Okay. That was your reward for ditching,

204
00:07:28,085 --> 00:07:29,865
但是既然你不喜欢
but if you don't want to...

205
00:07:31,365 --> 00:07:32,255
怎么回事
What "Uh-oh"?

206
00:07:32,325 --> 00:07:34,005
画面卡住了
Uh, it's frozen.

207
00:07:34,005 --> 00:07:34,945
什么
What?!

208
00:07:35,215 --> 00:07:35,795
我的天哪
Oh, my God.

209
00:07:35,795 --> 00:07:37,346
就停在这个恶心画面
It froze on that?

210
00:07:37,926 --> 00:07:39,436
你说的"恶心画面"是有名字的
Hey. "That" Has a name.

211
00:07:39,566 --> 00:07:42,006
来 斯黛拉 来吃吧 乖孩子
Here, Stella. Come and get it, girl.

212
00:07:42,116 --> 00:07:43,886
杰 是你吗
Jay, is that you?

213
00:07:43,886 --> 00:07:44,686
是的
Yep.

214
00:07:45,366 --> 00:07:46,746
该死
Damn it.

215
00:07:46,806 --> 00:07:47,766
该死
Damn it.

216
00:07:48,166 --> 00:07:49,376
-该死 -该死
- Damn it! - Damn it!

217
00:07:50,207 --> 00:07:52,627
-我没听见你进屋 -那就好
- I didn't hear you come in. - That's good.

218
00:07:53,337 --> 00:07:55,397
你怎么这么早就回来了
Oh, how come you're home so early?

219
00:07:55,397 --> 00:07:56,707
太累 不想打高尔夫
Too tired for golf.

220
00:07:56,797 --> 00:07:57,617
乔呢
Where's Joe?

221
00:07:57,617 --> 00:07:58,707
在楼上
Upstairs.

222
00:07:58,707 --> 00:08:00,707
我终于把他哄到睡着了
I finally got him to sleep.

223
00:08:02,017 --> 00:08:02,727
她想出去
She wants to get out.

224
00:08:02,727 --> 00:08:04,178
-我来抱她 -不 不 你待在这里
- I'll take her. - No, no, no. You stay here.

225
00:08:04,188 --> 00:08:05,658
-我把她抱出去 -不行
- I'll do it. - No, you can't.

226
00:08:06,058 --> 00:08:09,198
我是说 我们难得有独处的时间
I mean, w-we rarely get times like this anymore.

227
00:08:09,208 --> 00:08:12,208
乔在睡觉 曼尼也去上学了
Joe's sleeping, Manny is at school.

228
00:08:12,208 --> 00:08:13,708
不如我们上楼--
Why don't we go upstairs and --

229
00:08:13,708 --> 00:08:14,308
睡个午觉
Take a nap.

230
00:08:14,308 --> 00:08:15,498
没错
Exactly!

231
00:08:16,318 --> 00:08:17,479
我妈坐她朋友的车
My mom got picked up by a friend.

232
00:08:17,489 --> 00:08:18,949
我们可以开她的车去电脑店
We can take her car to the computer store

233
00:08:18,949 --> 00:08:20,189
在她回家前回来
and be back before she gets home.

234
00:08:21,939 --> 00:08:24,019
她没关窗也没关灯
She left the windows down and the lights on.

235
00:08:24,189 --> 00:08:26,609
有时她也太不注意了
Sometimes, she is so oblivious.

236
00:08:32,650 --> 00:08:35,670
我只要等杰睡着就好
All I had to do was wait for Jay to fall asleep.

237
00:08:35,670 --> 00:08:36,760
我简直是个天才
Genius.

238
00:08:39,430 --> 00:08:42,360
她几分钟内就会打呼的 太简单了
She'd be snoring in minutes. Piece of cake.

239
00:08:46,831 --> 00:08:48,991
我们离得也太远了
We are so far away from everything.

240
00:08:48,991 --> 00:08:51,141
他们上一次敬酒的时候 我在听到声音之前
During the last toast, I saw them clink the glasses

241
00:08:51,141 --> 00:08:53,251
先看到了他们的碰杯
before the sound actually reached us.

242
00:08:53,381 --> 00:08:54,581
婚礼被冷落
Snubbed at this wedding,

243
00:08:54,581 --> 00:08:55,941
其他两对的婚礼也没邀请我们...
not invited to two others...

244
00:08:55,941 --> 00:08:58,102
你究竟做了什么
what could you have possibly done?

245
00:09:00,262 --> 00:09:02,382
对不起 我说了会在吃甜品的时候跟你换位子
Sorry. I said I would switch with you at dessert.

246
00:09:02,382 --> 00:09:03,922
胡娇 胡娇
Oh, Pepper. Pepper.

247
00:09:03,922 --> 00:09:04,972
-你知不知道为什么... -不好意思
- Do you have any idea why... - Oh, sorry.

248
00:09:04,982 --> 00:09:06,952
我正赶着去土豆泥桌
I'm in a mad rush to the mashed-potato bar

249
00:09:06,952 --> 00:09:10,472
补一些 配食
to restock something called...fixin's.

250
00:09:11,072 --> 00:09:12,603
如果你们为我着想的话
If you ever felt anything for me,

251
00:09:12,603 --> 00:09:14,443
就把我扔出窗外吧
you'll push me out a window.

252
00:09:15,233 --> 00:09:17,533
米奇尔 可能...
You know, Mitchell, m-maybe it's...

253
00:09:18,213 --> 00:09:19,553
我不想争论这种事了
Look. I can't have this fight again.

254
00:09:19,563 --> 00:09:20,623
我看见你向他抛媚眼了
I saw you ogling him.

255
00:09:20,623 --> 00:09:21,893
对我来说
Hey, as far as I'm concerned,

256
00:09:21,893 --> 00:09:23,603
我们根本不应该再争论这种事
we never have to have this fight again.

257
00:09:23,603 --> 00:09:24,413
米奇尔 别
Mitchell, stop it.

258
00:09:24,413 --> 00:09:25,814
-怎么了 -偷听
- What? - Eavesdropping?

259
00:09:25,814 --> 00:09:26,804
寻求生意机会
Trolling for business?

260
00:09:26,804 --> 00:09:27,414
你一直这样
You've been doing it

261
00:09:27,414 --> 00:09:28,844
自从开始处理同性恋离婚案件
ever since you started handling gay divorce.

262
00:09:28,844 --> 00:09:29,774
这有点吓人
It's kind of ghoulish.

263
00:09:29,774 --> 00:09:31,154
-吓人 -没错
- Ghoulish? - Yes.

264
00:09:31,154 --> 00:09:33,064
肯定是因为这样才没人希望我们出现
I'll bet that's why nobody wants us around.

265
00:09:33,064 --> 00:09:36,274
就是这样 你就像是同性恋婚姻的死亡天使
That's it. You're like the Angel of Death of gay marriage.

266
00:09:36,454 --> 00:09:37,784
你就像老人家里的猫
You're like a cat at an old-folks' home

267
00:09:37,784 --> 00:09:39,695
在快死的人旁边蜷着
who curls up next to somebody about to die.

268
00:09:39,695 --> 00:09:41,155
他们还配谴责我吗
They're judging me?

269
00:09:41,595 --> 00:09:43,085
菲利克斯和乔丹可是做动物皮草生意的
Felix and Jordan sell fur.

270
00:09:43,085 --> 00:09:45,255
不好意思 我们不小心偷听到你们在偷听我们
Sorry. We couldn't help overhearing you overhearing us.

271
00:09:45,255 --> 00:09:46,745
我们的一些朋友正准备分手
Some friends of ours are breaking up,

272
00:09:46,745 --> 00:09:48,045
他们需要一位好的离婚律师
and they need a good divorce lawyer.

273
00:09:48,045 --> 00:09:48,945
你有名片吗
Do you have a card?

274
00:09:48,945 --> 00:09:50,005
我们不小心偷听到你们在说
We couldn't help overhearing you

275
00:09:50,005 --> 00:09:51,865
你们偷听到你们偷听你们
talking about you overhearing you overhearing you.

276
00:09:51,865 --> 00:09:54,516
你真的在接同性恋离婚案吗 我们都不知道
Are you really doing gay divorces now? We had no idea.

277
00:09:54,516 --> 00:09:56,006
我刚偷听到你们偷听...
I was just overhearing you guys overhearing...

278
00:09:56,006 --> 00:09:58,486
我的天 这叽里呱啦的
Good Lord, it's like a game of Princess Telephone.

279
00:09:58,486 --> 00:10:01,536
这是我的名片 我想问一下
Here is my card, and just to be clear,

280
00:10:01,536 --> 00:10:03,936
你们没有人知道我在接同性恋离婚案吗
none of you knew I was doing gay divorces?

281
00:10:04,096 --> 00:10:04,946
-不知道 -有点意思
- No. - Oh, interesting.

282
00:10:04,946 --> 00:10:06,947
太有意思了 婚礼上玩得愉快
That's very interesting. Have a good time at the wedding.

283
00:10:07,967 --> 00:10:09,807
原来这份吓人的职业
Well, how about this ghoulish profession

284
00:10:09,807 --> 00:10:12,367
除了你之外所有人都觉得没问题
that no one seems to have a problem with except for you?

285
00:10:12,367 --> 00:10:15,307
对不起 但你一直都有点愤世嫉俗
Look, I'm sorry, but you've always been a little cynical,

286
00:10:15,307 --> 00:10:18,427
我担心你看多了这些婚姻失败的案子
and I was worried you seeing all these marriages collapse

287
00:10:18,427 --> 00:10:19,958
会让你不由得往那个方向发展
would push you further in that direction.

288
00:10:19,958 --> 00:10:21,518
不 不 恰恰相反
No, no, it's the opposite.

289
00:10:21,518 --> 00:10:22,998
在这些不幸夫妻身边
Being around all these unhappy couples

290
00:10:23,008 --> 00:10:25,588
让我对我们所拥有的更加感激
makes me even more grateful for what we have.

291
00:10:25,738 --> 00:10:26,828
太感动了 你...
That's so sweet. Are...

292
00:10:27,088 --> 00:10:29,148
你确定这不是你酒喝多了随便说的吗
are you sure that's not the cash bar talking?

293
00:10:29,148 --> 00:10:30,168
当然不是
Of course not.

294
00:10:30,168 --> 00:10:33,059
你是我所遇过最好的事
You're the best thing that has ever happened to me.

295
00:10:33,769 --> 00:10:35,729
你也是我所遇过最好的事
And you're the best thing that's ever happened to me.

296
00:10:35,749 --> 00:10:36,539
小卡
Oh, Cam.

297
00:10:36,539 --> 00:10:38,229
也许这才是没人希望我们出现的原因
Maybe this is why nobody wants us around

298
00:10:38,229 --> 00:10:40,809
因为我们去到那里都那么感性
is because we cause an emotional scene everywhere we go.

299
00:10:40,809 --> 00:10:42,169
对不起
I'm sorry.

300
00:10:42,529 --> 00:10:44,659
我永远都不会成为他想要的儿子
I'll never be the son he wants.

301
00:10:45,639 --> 00:10:47,530
我们会变成什么样
What's to become of us?

302
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:51,220
现在可真是难倒我了
Well, now I'm stumped.

303
00:10:52,050 --> 00:10:53,860
没错 那可以冷藏东西
Yep. That refrigerates stuff.

304
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:54,870
它们都可以
All of them do.

305
00:10:54,870 --> 00:10:55,980
俗话说得好
But you know the saying...

306
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:58,540
所有好的开放参观日都要在两点准时结束
All good open houses must come to an end by 2:00 on the dot.

307
00:10:58,540 --> 00:11:01,251
可是我妈妈还在来的路上
Oh, but my mom's still on her way.

308
00:11:01,251 --> 00:11:02,671
她要来给首期
She's giving us our down payment.

309
00:11:02,671 --> 00:11:04,541
你嫁给一个鼓手的时候就知道要怎么做了
You knew the rules when you married a drummer.

310
00:11:06,471 --> 00:11:07,661
我们妨碍到你了吗
Are we keeping you from something?

311
00:11:07,661 --> 00:11:09,491
一"拍"都没有
Not one "beat."

312
00:11:09,611 --> 00:11:10,691
我有个主意
I have an idea.

313
00:11:10,691 --> 00:11:12,471
要不我们用刚出炉纸杯蛋糕的香味
Why don't we greet your mom

314
00:11:12,471 --> 00:11:14,732
来迎接你妈妈吧
with the smell of fresh-baked cupcakes?

315
00:11:14,732 --> 00:11:15,952
材料在这里
The ingredients are in here.

316
00:11:15,952 --> 00:11:16,852
威尔 拿好搅拌器
Will, grab a whisk.

317
00:11:16,852 --> 00:11:19,452
我会在你们俩撒糖霜之前回来
I'll be back before you two are frosting.

318
00:11:20,442 --> 00:11:22,062
我在去取的路上 斯坦
I'm on my way to pick it up, Stan.

319
00:11:22,062 --> 00:11:23,742
我会在5...
I'll be there in like 5...

320
00:11:23,812 --> 00:11:26,742
至45分钟到
to 45 minutes.

321
00:11:26,962 --> 00:11:29,183
好吧 纸杯蛋糕
Okay. Cupcakes.

322
00:11:29,183 --> 00:11:31,423
礼 不 不
Pres...Oh, no. No.

323
00:11:31,423 --> 00:11:32,533
该死
Damn it.

324
00:11:34,333 --> 00:11:35,823
纸杯蛋糕烤糊了
The cupcakes burned.

325
00:11:36,063 --> 00:11:37,903
闻起来还不错
Well, it still smells homey.

326
00:11:38,313 --> 00:11:39,673
给了妈妈一个机会好好看看
And it gives Mom a chance

327
00:11:39,683 --> 00:11:43,484
这里最先进的烟雾报警器是如何工作的
to see how well this state-of-the-art smoke alarm works!

328
00:11:43,544 --> 00:11:44,394
跟我来 妈妈
Come with me, Mom!

329
00:11:44,404 --> 00:11:46,954
让我带你看看这幢好房子的其他部分
Let me show you around the rest of this dream house!

330
00:11:47,064 --> 00:11:49,014
看到没 连熨衣服都是一种享受
You see, even ironing is a delight here,

331
00:11:49,014 --> 00:11:51,024
你可以感受到从滑窗外
where you can feel a cool breeze

332
00:11:51,024 --> 00:11:53,544
拂进来的微风
wafting in from the open sliders.

333
00:11:53,544 --> 00:11:54,705
我了个去
Mother nature!

334
00:11:54,715 --> 00:11:56,845
你瞧 专属的礼物包装室
Huzzah! Your own gift-wrapping room,

335
00:11:56,845 --> 00:11:58,265
就像富人和名人家里的一样
just like the rich and famous.

336
00:11:58,265 --> 00:11:59,555
席拉 借我根手指
Sheila, finger.

337
00:12:00,665 --> 00:12:02,315
来吧 好的
Go right ahead. There we go.

338
00:12:02,325 --> 00:12:05,185
不好意思我来晚了 但别担心
Sorry I'm late, guys, but fear not.

339
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:08,196
一份生日礼物
One birthday present.

340
00:12:08,196 --> 00:12:09,376
包装得像婴儿礼物一样
Wrapped in baby-shower paper.

341
00:12:09,376 --> 00:12:11,566
一件熨好服帖的礼裙
One crisply pressed dress.

342
00:12:11,566 --> 00:12:13,846
上边有一个之前没有的褶子
With one big pleat it didn't used to have.

343
00:12:14,006 --> 00:12:15,546
至少我们知道你为什么迟到了
At least we know why you were late.

344
00:12:15,546 --> 00:12:17,106
看起来你好像是从一个着火的面包店里
Looks like you rescued those cupcakes

345
00:12:17,106 --> 00:12:18,346
救出来的那些纸杯蛋糕
from a burning bakery.

346
00:12:18,346 --> 00:12:19,926
别担心 妈妈做了那些备用的蛋糕
Don't worry. Mom made those on the off chance

347
00:12:19,936 --> 00:12:22,297
以防万一你搞砸了 果然不出所料
what everyone knew was gonna happen happened.

348
00:12:22,297 --> 00:12:23,877
她还给我买了那条新裙子
She also bought me that new dress.

349
00:12:24,217 --> 00:12:26,007
对了 希望你留了发票
Oh, and I hope you kept the receipt,

350
00:12:26,007 --> 00:12:27,197
因为妈妈给我买了备用的礼物
because Mom bought a backup.

351
00:12:27,207 --> 00:12:30,317
好吧 别因为妈妈低估我就生她的气
Well, don't be mad at your mom for underestimating me.

352
00:12:30,317 --> 00:12:31,467
我们怎么可能生气呢
Oh, how could we, when she made us

353
00:12:31,467 --> 00:12:32,787
她还给我们做了手工搅拌冰激凌
this fresh hand-churned ice cream?

354
00:12:32,787 --> 00:12:33,457
怎么可能
Yeah. What?

355
00:12:33,457 --> 00:12:34,497
对了 你知道我们该怎么做吗
Oh, you know what we should do?

356
00:12:34,497 --> 00:12:36,048
我们应该给她发一张我们吃冰激凌的照片
We should send her a picture of us eating it.

357
00:12:36,048 --> 00:12:37,618
看来我回家至少还能给你们拍张照片
I guess it's a good thing I came home when I did.

358
00:12:37,618 --> 00:12:38,758
还是我来拍比较好
It'd be better if I did it.

359
00:12:41,808 --> 00:12:42,768
你做了冰激凌
You churned ice cream?

360
00:12:42,778 --> 00:12:44,438
是的 孩子们喜欢吗
Yeah. Did the kids like it?

361
00:12:44,438 --> 00:12:45,668
-她们爱死了 -太棒了
- They loved it. - Great.

362
00:12:45,678 --> 00:12:47,568
但是她们知道我不会做冰激凌
But they know I can't make ice cream.

363
00:12:47,668 --> 00:12:49,959
我是喝了三杯血腥玛丽之后看了购物广告
I bought that churn out of a SkyMall catalog

364
00:12:49,959 --> 00:12:51,539
才买的那个搅拌器
after three Bloody Marys.

365
00:12:51,539 --> 00:12:54,399
它在我车库里一块布下面盖了六年了
It's been sitting under a tarp in my garage for six years.

366
00:12:54,399 --> 00:12:56,469
你可得多收敛收敛了
You've got to dial it way back.

367
00:12:56,469 --> 00:12:58,129
你为什么要害怕跟生气呢
Where is this fear and anger coming from?

368
00:12:58,129 --> 00:13:00,099
你会害我们被发现的
You're gonna get us caught!

369
00:13:01,129 --> 00:13:03,590
一开始你就知道这是有风险的
You knew the risks when we started this.

370
00:13:03,590 --> 00:13:06,280
我只是说我们最近有点马虎了
I'm just saying we're getting a little bit sloppy.

371
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:08,910
所有那些不可能的差事 精致的三明治
All the impossible errands, the fancy sandwiches.

372
00:13:08,910 --> 00:13:11,510
接下来的几天只要在全麦面包上涂点
Just slap a little tuna on whole wheat

373
00:13:11,510 --> 00:13:12,410
-吞拿鱼就够了 -你说什么 不行
- for the next couple of days. - What? N--

374
00:13:12,410 --> 00:13:15,310
先等事情平息一段时间
Just until things cool off.

375
00:13:15,350 --> 00:13:16,351
好吗
All right?

376
00:13:18,521 --> 00:13:20,021
我只是想让你开心点
I was just trying to make you happy.

377
00:13:22,721 --> 00:13:24,301
你不会阻止我的 是吗
You're not gonna stop me, are you?

378
00:13:24,541 --> 00:13:26,981
咖啡车只在大厅服务到四点
Coffee cart's only in the lobby until 4:00.

379
00:13:27,811 --> 00:13:28,761
谢谢你 克莱尔
Thank you, Claire.

380
00:13:29,722 --> 00:13:30,502
谢谢
Thank you.

381
00:13:31,402 --> 00:13:32,492
这太没面子了
This is mortifying.

382
00:13:32,502 --> 00:13:33,612
修它的人会看到我们看的东西
Whoever we ask to fix this

383
00:13:33,612 --> 00:13:35,922
觉得我们是变态
is gonna see what we're watching and think we're pervs.

384
00:13:35,922 --> 00:13:37,142
那个人就不会
Not that guy.

385
00:13:37,332 --> 00:13:38,342
卢克
Luke?!

386
00:13:40,972 --> 00:13:42,172
你好啊 玛丽安
Hi, Marianne.

387
00:13:44,403 --> 00:13:45,783
你都长这么大了
You're so grown-up now.

388
00:13:45,783 --> 00:13:47,873
是啊 这是曼尼
Yeah. Uh, this is Manny.

389
00:13:47,873 --> 00:13:49,533
玛丽安以前是我们的保姆
Marianne used to be our babysitter.

390
00:13:49,533 --> 00:13:51,363
还记得以前你跟我求婚吗
Remember when you asked me to marry you?

391
00:13:51,363 --> 00:13:52,873
"我外[爱]你 玛丽安"
"I wuv you, Marianne."

392
00:13:53,433 --> 00:13:55,293
很高兴见到你 我们得走了
Well, nice to meet you. We should get going.

393
00:13:55,293 --> 00:13:57,424
好吧 再见了 给家里带好
Okay. Bye, guys. Best to your family, okay?

394
00:13:58,604 --> 00:14:00,784
我真想看看知道你堕落成这样之后
I'd like to see the look on Mawianne's face

395
00:14:00,784 --> 00:14:02,724
玛丽安脸上会是什么表情
if she knew what a degenerate you turned into.

396
00:14:02,724 --> 00:14:03,864
下一个
Next.

397
00:14:03,864 --> 00:14:04,734
我来吧 凯尔
I'm here, Kyle.

398
00:14:06,714 --> 00:14:07,814
又见面了
Hello again.

399
00:14:07,844 --> 00:14:08,774
我能帮你们做什么
How can I help?

400
00:14:11,245 --> 00:14:13,815
我们要怎么办 我妈随时都会回来的
What are we gonna do? Mom's gonna be home any minute.

401
00:14:13,815 --> 00:14:15,975
"亲爱的 你看到我的电脑了吗"
"Hola, papi. Have you seen my computer?"

402
00:14:15,975 --> 00:14:17,135
"当然了 妈妈 就在那
"Oh, sure, Mom. It's over there,

403
00:14:17,135 --> 00:14:18,275
有个没穿衣服的女孩正在里边
where that naked girl's entertaining

404
00:14:18,275 --> 00:14:19,575
取悦她学校的篮球队员呢"
her school's basketball team."

405
00:14:19,575 --> 00:14:20,805
我跟艾丽克斯视频一下
I'm face-timing Alex.

406
00:14:20,805 --> 00:14:21,905
她会知道怎么办
She'll know what to do.

407
00:14:21,905 --> 00:14:22,675
怎么了 卢克
What's up, Luke?

408
00:14:22,675 --> 00:14:24,496
电脑出了点小问题 屏幕不动了
Computer glitch. The screen's frozen.

409
00:14:24,496 --> 00:14:26,266
-让我看看 -还是不要了
- Let me see. - I'd rather not.

410
00:14:26,266 --> 00:14:27,356
所以是黄片
So porn.

411
00:14:27,456 --> 00:14:28,546
好吧 我先把这篇论文写完
Well, I just have to finish this paper.

412
00:14:28,546 --> 00:14:29,736
我一小时后打给你
I'll call you in an hour.

413
00:14:29,736 --> 00:14:31,576
你好呀 小可爱
Oh, hey there, cutie pie.

414
00:14:31,576 --> 00:14:32,966
谢谢夸奖 艾丽克斯 但你能快点写
Thank you, Alex, but could you please hurry

415
00:14:32,966 --> 00:14:34,306
-然后给我们回电话吗 -我是和
- and call us back? - I was talk--

416
00:14:35,336 --> 00:14:36,976
她知道我对她而言就是禁果
She knows I'm forbidden fruit.

417
00:14:36,976 --> 00:14:38,477
我确信她因此更被我吸引了
I'm sure that's half the appeal.

418
00:14:53,648 --> 00:14:54,568
杰
Jay!

419
00:14:55,068 --> 00:14:56,098
杰
Jay?

420
00:14:59,188 --> 00:15:01,208
你醒了多久了
How long since you have been up?

421
00:15:01,208 --> 00:15:03,248
我醒了没多久
Oh, about a minute before you.

422
00:15:03,448 --> 00:15:05,059
你能帮我个忙吗
Oh, can you do me a favor?

423
00:15:05,059 --> 00:15:06,759
你能不能去看看洗的衣服
Can you go and look at the laundry?

424
00:15:06,759 --> 00:15:07,669
我觉得好像洗好了
I think it's done.

425
00:15:07,669 --> 00:15:09,329
当然了 但是亲爱的 我睡得有点不舒服
Sure, but, honey, I think I slept kind of weird.

426
00:15:09,329 --> 00:15:12,019
你能去楼上帮我把加热垫拿下来吗
Could you run back upstairs and get me my heating pad?

427
00:15:13,369 --> 00:15:15,129
斯黛拉为什么拼命要去那里
Why is Stella going crazy there?

428
00:15:15,129 --> 00:15:16,489
斯黛拉 快走开
Stella, get out of here!

429
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:20,870
你们好 大家都怎么样啊
Hi, there. How's everybody doing?

430
00:15:21,090 --> 00:15:21,890
斯黛拉怎么了
What's up with Stella?

431
00:15:21,890 --> 00:15:22,980
你们俩去哪了
Where have you two been?

432
00:15:23,810 --> 00:15:24,910
那是我的电脑吗
Is that my computer?!

433
00:15:24,910 --> 00:15:26,550
-别打开它 -别打开它
- Don't open that! - Don't open that!

434
00:15:27,270 --> 00:15:28,820
-那是乔的飞机吗 -别开门
- Is that Joe's plane? - Don't open that!

435
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:33,851
看起来这有不少未解之谜啊
A lot of unanswered questions here, it seems like.

436
00:15:34,191 --> 00:15:37,951
我看我们都先各退一步
Why don't we all just...take a step back?

437
00:15:38,271 --> 00:15:40,811
放轻松
Nice and easy.

438
00:15:42,191 --> 00:15:43,371
好了 所以
Okay, so...

439
00:15:45,152 --> 00:15:48,032
我现在要出去散个步
now I am going to go and take a little walk.

440
00:15:49,762 --> 00:15:52,402
卢克和我要上楼做作业
Luke and I have some homework to do upstairs.

441
00:15:52,402 --> 00:15:56,292
而我 要去小朋友的房间
And I'm going... to the little boy's room.

442
00:16:01,423 --> 00:16:04,243
除了我们这里 他们每桌都拍了照片
They have taken pictures at every table but ours.

443
00:16:04,243 --> 00:16:06,503
因为他们的摄影师不是黛安·阿勃斯
Because their photographer isn't Diane Arbus.

444
00:16:06,503 --> 00:16:08,973
不然还有谁愿意记录这场《热夜之梦》
Who else would want a record of this Fever Dream?

445
00:16:09,393 --> 00:16:10,643
你还要吃这个吗
Are you gonna finish this?

446
00:16:10,643 --> 00:16:12,404
他们没准备工作餐
They didn't budget a staff meal.

447
00:16:12,514 --> 00:16:14,194
我们穷是我们自己的错
It's our own fault we're poor.

448
00:16:14,344 --> 00:16:15,584
我们有钱的时候
When we had money,

449
00:16:15,584 --> 00:16:16,964
把钱都花来雇喝醉的水手了
we spent it all on drunken sailors.

450
00:16:16,964 --> 00:16:18,774
你是想说"像喝醉的水手一样花钱"吧
You mean "like drunken sailors"?

451
00:16:18,794 --> 00:16:19,614
当然了
Sure.

452
00:16:19,614 --> 00:16:21,374
胡娇 你走之前
Pepper, before you run off again,

453
00:16:21,374 --> 00:16:23,794
为什么所有人都当我们像贱民一样
why is almost everyone here treating us like pariahs?

454
00:16:23,794 --> 00:16:26,165
你们不是冰冷地拒绝了
Well, you didn't help yourselves by the cold way

455
00:16:26,165 --> 00:16:28,385
前两个婚礼邀请吗
you declined those last two wedding invitations.

456
00:16:28,385 --> 00:16:29,775
我们没有收到邀请啊
We didn't get those invitations.

457
00:16:29,775 --> 00:16:31,435
但我收到你们的回复了啊
I got the RSVPs myself

458
00:16:31,445 --> 00:16:33,155
给亚当和迈克以及菲利克斯和乔丹的回复
to Adam and Michael and Felix and Jordan.

459
00:16:33,155 --> 00:16:36,205
只在"无法出席"那一栏画了个大叉
Just a big "X" In the "Will Not Attend" Box.

460
00:16:36,265 --> 00:16:38,025
没有理由 没有礼物
No excuse, no gift.

461
00:16:38,195 --> 00:16:39,686
你当然可以引起别人的不快
Of course you put people off.

462
00:16:39,686 --> 00:16:40,906
只是这并没什么风度
It's just not classy.

463
00:16:43,786 --> 00:16:45,926
这些布丁得放了多少天了
How old are these pudding cups?!

464
00:16:46,336 --> 00:16:46,946
过来 亲爱的
Come, carino.

465
00:16:46,946 --> 00:16:48,756
在大厅里有个自动售货机
There's a vending machine in the lobby.

466
00:16:48,756 --> 00:16:50,186
如果我在它旁边倒下了
If I lie down next to it,

467
00:16:50,196 --> 00:16:52,056
你会把它推到我身上让我死吗
will you push it over on me?

468
00:16:52,496 --> 00:16:55,327
为什么我们回复了从未收到的婚礼邀请函
How could we RSVP to wedding invitations that we never got?

469
00:16:55,327 --> 00:16:58,247
参加聚会的人们 让我们跳起来吧
Okay, party people, on your feet.

470
00:16:58,247 --> 00:16:59,617
如果我提前离开 你俩有意见吗
You guys cool if I take off?

471
00:16:59,617 --> 00:17:01,337
不 亲爱的 你怎么了
No. Sweetie, what's been going on with you?

472
00:17:01,337 --> 00:17:02,957
自从我们到这你就想着走
You've wanted to leave since we got here.

473
00:17:03,157 --> 00:17:04,137
你们都去跳舞吗
Hey, y'all coming?

474
00:17:04,597 --> 00:17:05,547
管它呢 去跳吧
Might as well.

475
00:17:05,547 --> 00:17:06,938
走啦 莉莉 我们去跳舞
Come on, Lily. Let's go dance.

476
00:17:06,938 --> 00:17:09,088
不 不跳 这太尴尬了
No! No dancing. It's too embarrassing.

477
00:17:09,088 --> 00:17:11,738
不是的 你跳得非常棒 亲爱的
No. You're a good dancer, sweetie.

478
00:17:11,738 --> 00:17:13,648
不是说我 说你们呢
Not me. You two.

479
00:17:13,648 --> 00:17:14,198
什么
What?

480
00:17:14,198 --> 00:17:16,678
你不喜欢我们跳舞 为什么
You don't like our dancing? Why?

481
00:17:16,718 --> 00:17:17,738
还问为什么
Why?

482
00:17:25,919 --> 00:17:28,519
你们跳得并不好 所以我讨厌婚礼
You're not good. That's why I hate weddings.

483
00:17:28,519 --> 00:17:30,699
等等 莉莉 你是不是回复了一些婚礼邀请
Wait, Lily, did you RSVP to some weddings

484
00:17:30,699 --> 00:17:31,509
却没有告诉我们
and not tell us?

485
00:17:31,509 --> 00:17:33,259
是的 惩罚我吧 给我禁足吧
Yes. Punish me, ground me.

486
00:17:33,259 --> 00:17:34,780
我就是不想看你俩跳舞的丑态了
I just can't watch it again.

487
00:17:34,780 --> 00:17:35,860
你绝对会被惩罚的
Oh, you're gonna be punished.

488
00:17:35,860 --> 00:17:37,770
米奇尔 等一下 我理解她的感受
Mitchell, wait. I know how she feels.

489
00:17:37,770 --> 00:17:39,350
我俩真的令你那么难堪吗
Did we really embarrass you that bad?

490
00:17:39,360 --> 00:17:42,400
是的 我依然爱你们 但
Well, yeah. I mean, I still love you, but...

491
00:17:43,050 --> 00:17:44,730
为什么你的肩膀在动
Why are your shoulders moving?

492
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:45,490
我们一直知道
Well, we always knew there

493
00:17:45,490 --> 00:17:47,020
我们俩有某些地方让你厌烦
would be something you didn't like about us.

494
00:17:47,020 --> 00:17:47,911
我们只是很高兴
We're just glad that

495
00:17:47,911 --> 00:17:49,951
令你不快的竟是我们如此擅长的事情
it's something we're so good at.

496
00:17:56,911 --> 00:17:59,591
如果有人问起 就说我是和你们一起来的
If anybody asks, I'm with you.

497
00:18:02,182 --> 00:18:03,942
是的 加文 我准备好了你要的
Yes, Gavin, I got everything you asked for,

498
00:18:03,942 --> 00:18:04,982
而且我马上到
and I'm on my way.

499
00:18:05,212 --> 00:18:06,812
我要给老板做这么多跑腿的事
All these errands I have to do for my boss.

500
00:18:06,812 --> 00:18:08,102
我发誓如果要不是因为我
I swear, if it wasn't for me,

501
00:18:08,102 --> 00:18:08,992
他什么也弄不好
he'd never get anything.

502
00:18:08,992 --> 00:18:10,782
海莉 拜托 我正试图弄清
Haley, please. I'm trying to figure out

503
00:18:10,782 --> 00:18:13,632
你妈妈是如何自己完成那么多事的
how your mom's getting all these things done by yourself.

504
00:18:13,732 --> 00:18:16,333
当海莉给了我一个倾听自己心声的机会
When Haley finally gave me a chance to hear myself think,

505
00:18:16,333 --> 00:18:17,443
我突然想到了
it hit me.

506
00:18:17,623 --> 00:18:19,373
会不会是克莱尔请了个助手
Could Claire be using an assistant?

507
00:18:19,373 --> 00:18:22,843
我决定追溯今天她说的每件差事
I decided to retrace every errand she allegedly ran today

508
00:18:22,843 --> 00:18:24,173
并且计算时间
and time it out.

509
00:18:24,203 --> 00:18:27,463
从早上九点到下午一点半她在开会
She was in meetings from 9:00 A.M. To 1:30,

510
00:18:27,673 --> 00:18:30,724
假设她有九十分钟来买海莉的裙子
leaving her a 90-minute window to buy Haley's dress,

511
00:18:30,724 --> 00:18:33,884
到商场找斯坦取艾丽克斯的礼物
see Stan at Best Buy for Alex's present,

512
00:18:33,884 --> 00:18:36,004
然后开车回家
then speed home,

513
00:18:36,194 --> 00:18:38,494
然后她可以开始烤纸杯蛋糕
where she could start baking the cupcakes,

514
00:18:38,494 --> 00:18:40,924
从车库里把冰淇淋搅拌器搬出来
drag the churn in from the garage,

515
00:18:40,944 --> 00:18:45,075
搅拌 包装 上霜
churn, wrap, and frost,

516
00:18:45,075 --> 00:18:47,405
她还剩不到八分钟在学校放学路段拥挤的时刻
leaving her a scant eight minutes at school pick-up time

517
00:18:47,405 --> 00:18:50,125
加速赶回公司参加三点的员工会议
to race back for her 3:00 staff meeting.

518
00:18:50,125 --> 00:18:53,345
即使在她路上全部十四盏交通灯都是绿的
Even if all 14 traffic lights on her route were green,

519
00:18:53,345 --> 00:18:54,915
这项任务也会是
this task would be...

520
00:18:55,216 --> 00:18:56,516
不可能完成的
Impossible.

521
00:18:57,016 --> 00:18:58,726
我不知道冰激凌是谁做的
I don't know who made that ice cream,

522
00:18:59,256 --> 00:19:01,436
但是爸爸我即将在一个满是霜冻的大碗掀起风暴
but Daddy was about to churn up a frosty bowl

523
00:19:01,436 --> 00:19:02,926
这个碗就叫"妈妈是个大骗子"
of "Mom's A Big Fake."

524
00:19:04,506 --> 00:19:06,736
本 你还在这里做什么
Ben, what are you still doing here?

525
00:19:06,736 --> 00:19:08,196
